                            <comment id="17234543" author="alex_pl" created="Wed, 18 Nov 2020 12:12:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ptupitsyn&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ptupitsyn&quot;&gt;ptupitsyn&lt;/a&gt;, I don&apos;t think it&apos;s blocked by &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13496&quot; title=&quot;Java thin: Use non-blocking socket IO &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-13496&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-13496&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, I think it can be relatively easy fixed by waiting for future &lt;tt&gt;pendingReq&lt;/tt&gt; with timeout in &lt;tt&gt;TcpClientChannel#receive&lt;/tt&gt; instead of timeout on socket. Also, patch can be included to 2.9.1 scope.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17234573" author="ptupitsyn" created="Wed, 18 Nov 2020 12:40:09 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alex_pl&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alex_pl&quot;&gt;alex_pl&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13496&quot; title=&quot;Java thin: Use non-blocking socket IO &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-13496&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-13496&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; will fix this problem anyway, so I thought we can skip a dedicated fix, that&apos;s why I linked it as &quot;blocked by&quot;.&lt;br/&gt;
Please feel free to take this ticket if you&apos;d like to do the fix.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17235423" author="alex_pl" created="Thu, 19 Nov 2020 12:44:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ptupitsyn&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ptupitsyn&quot;&gt;ptupitsyn&lt;/a&gt;, yes, it will be fixed by &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13496&quot; title=&quot;Java thin: Use non-blocking socket IO &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-13496&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-13496&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, but in 2.10 or later. I propose a simple fix (see attached PR). After &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13496&quot; title=&quot;Java thin: Use non-blocking socket IO &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-13496&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-13496&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; at least tests from this fix can be reused. Can you please do a review?  &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
